PART 1: THE SELF-LOOP FRACTION — WHAT IT MEASURES
------------------------------------------------------------

  The self-loop fraction = probability that a random arc flip
  stays in the SAME isomorphism class.

  This measures: how much of the arc-flip operation is "wasted"
  (produces an isomorphic tournament, i.e., just relabeling).

  Equivalently: self-loop fraction = label redundancy per flip.

  n=3: self-loop fraction = 0.500
    Total flips: 24
    Self-flips (stay in class): ~12
    External flips (change class): ~12

  n=4: self-loop fraction = 0.375
    Total flips: 384
    Self-flips (stay in class): ~144
    External flips (change class): ~240

  n=5: self-loop fraction = 0.172
    Total flips: 10,240
    Self-flips (stay in class): ~1,761
    External flips (change class): ~8,478

  n=6: self-loop fraction = 0.077
    Total flips: 491,520
    Self-flips (stay in class): ~37,847
    External flips (change class): ~453,672

  THE SELF-LOOP FRACTION MEASURES THE AVERAGE AUTOMORPHISM DENSITY:

  SELF-LOOP FRACTION vs 1/n (approximate Aut density):
    n=3: self-loop = 0.5000, 1/n = 0.3333, ratio = 1.500
    n=4: self-loop = 0.3750, 1/n = 0.2500, ratio = 1.500
    n=5: self-loop = 0.1720, 1/n = 0.2000, ratio = 0.860
    n=6: self-loop = 0.0770, 1/n = 0.1667, ratio = 0.462

  The self-loop fraction decreases FASTER than 1/n.
  It's closer to 1/n! × (something).


